// A call given one argument too many deep in a chain of calls is an error
// said at once. Each call of the chain reads its arguments again when the
// generics it took from the expected type do not fit, and an argument that
// failed against a type with nothing left to infer is not read again: the
// work grows with the depth of the chain, not twice per level.

@ cases.over-applied-cons-deep-in-a-chain
source = ```tauto
